Subject: [PATCH 5.15.y 0/2] can: isotp: backport of 2 patches that failed to
 apply to 5.15-stable

This resubmits "can: isotp: fix use-after-free race with concurrent
NETDEV_UNREGISTER" (commit 20bab8b88baac140ca3701116e1d486c7f51e311
upstream), which failed to apply to the 5.15-stable tree, together
with "can: isotp: serialize TX state transitions under so->rx_lock"
(commit cf070fe33bfbd1a4c21236078fadb35dd223a157 upstream) from the
same upstream series, which builds on it and would otherwise fail
for the same reason. This is the full set of 3 upstream isotp.c
patches from 7.2-rc3 minus the 1 already queued by the normal stable
process for 5.15 ("can: isotp: use unconditional synchronize_rcu()
in isotp_release()").

Same scope as linux-5.10.y, with one difference: 5.15-stable already
carries the sk_error_report() wrapper throughout isotp.c (unlike
5.10, which still calls sk->sk_error_report(sk) directly), so
isotp_tx_timeout() applies unmodified here. isotp_init() still needs
adaptation for the same two independent, not-backported prerequisites
as on 5.10.y: the dynamic max_pdu_size TX buffer resize (commits
2f2dd39 "can: isotp: set max PDU size to 64 kByte", 2022, and
973bb01 "can: isotp: add module parameter for maximum pdu size",
2023, neither Cc: stable) and the hrtimer_setup() API consolidation.
The corresponding hunks are omitted or adapted to the older code
shape; the actual race fixes themselves are unaffected and fully
applied. See each patch's changelog for the exact adaptation.

Patch 1/2 ("fix use-after-free race with concurrent
NETDEV_UNREGISTER") is additionally adapted: upstream uses the
netdevice_tracker/netdev_hold()/netdev_put() debug-tracking infra,
which is not available on 5.15-stable. Replaced with the plain,
always-available dev_hold()/dev_put(), which is functionally
identical for the actual fix (holding a reference across a
concurrent NETDEV_UNREGISTER) - just without the extra leak-tracking
instrumentation. This mirrors the same adaptation made to the bcm.c
patch series and to isotp.c on 5.10.y, after an actual build failure
was reported there ("error: unknown type name 'netdevice_tracker'");
this revision has been verified with a clean git am against a seeded
net/can/isotp.c and no longer references that type anywhere in the
result.

This assumes the 1 already-queued isotp.c patch for 5.15-stable has
landed by the time this is applied. If not, please let me know and I
will rebase.

